      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U6-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The TPS62933 buck regulator U6 has its EN pin (pin 2) on net unconnected-(U6-EN-Pad2) with no other connections.",
      "expected": "The EN pin should be tied to VIN (+24V) or a control signal to enable the regulator, per the TPS62933 datasheet and standard practice for always-on operation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"148\") (name \"unconnected-(U6-EN-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 24V→5V buck will not start, so the +5V and +3V3 rails will be absent, rendering the board non-functional.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a critical open connection: the enable pin of the TPS62933 buck regulator (U6.2) is left floating, which prevents the 5V rail from coming up and disables the board."
}

